# 🐚 Day 19 – Shell Scripting Cheat Sheet

## 1. `find` Command ⭐⭐⭐

`find` is heavily used in Linux administration and automation.

### Find `.log` files

```bash
find /var/log -name "*.log" -type f
```

### Find files older than 7 days

```bash
find /var/log -name "*.log" -type f -mtime +7
```

### Find `.gz` files older than 30 days

```bash
find /var/log -name "*.gz" -type f -mtime +30
```

### Delete old files

```bash
find /backup -name "*.tar.gz" -type f -mtime +14 -delete
```

⚠️ Be careful with `-delete` in production. Always test the `find` command without `-delete` first.

