# 2. `gzip` ⭐⭐

Compress a file:

```bash
gzip application.log
```

This normally produces:

```text
application.log.gz
```

Decompress:

```bash
gunzip application.log.gz
```

Check compressed file:

```bash
ls -lh application.log.gz
```

---

# 3. `tar` Backup ⭐⭐⭐

Create compressed archive:

```bash
tar -czf backup.tar.gz /source/dir
```

Options:

```text
-c → create
-z → gzip compression
-f → archive filename
```

Extract:

```bash
tar -xzf backup.tar.gz
```

List contents:

```bash
tar -tzf backup.tar.gz
```

### Very useful interview point

```text
tar
 ↓
Archive multiple files/directories

gzip
 ↓
Compress data

tar -czf
 ↓
Create a gzip-compressed tar archive
```

